    <name>
      <text>9.2 Factorising - common factor, indices and difference of two squares</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[/*Part (a)  */
<p>Fully factorise the following expressions:</p>
<p>(a) {@expr1@} = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><i>You can use ^ to write powers</i></p>
<p>(b) {@expr2@} = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) {@expr3@} = [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
